Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:00:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(certify): no join cuts in a scoped dispatcher

A segment that starts at a cut configuration starts from an arbitrary
stack, so where the selector word is still on the stack, before the
dispatcher's last excluded case, the scope's hypotheses on the call's
selector no longer prune the excluded functions: the segment evaluates
their bodies and fails or runs out of heartbeats. Under --exclude, the
blocks from which an excluded case is reachable are no longer join or
bound_segments cut points (loops still cut them). For UniswapV2Pair's
getReserves() this keeps inline-returns' dispatcher in one segment,
which then checks in 80 s.
---
 solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 34 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py b/solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py
index bb430eeb..079b95c4 100644
--- a/solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py
+++ b/solar-tv/milestone/cutpoints.py
@@ -437,8 +437,12 @@ def evm_call_cuts(pass_name, a_blocks, b_blocks):
     b_ids = [i for i, _ in b_blocks]
     common = {i for i in a_ids if a_ids.count(i) == 1 and b_ids.count(i) == 1}
     sides = []
+    # Blocks of either program at or before the dispatcher's excluded cases: never join or
+    # bound cuts (dispatch_closure).
+    dispatch = set()
     for blocks, ids in ((a_blocks, a_ids), (b_blocks, b_ids)):
         edges = scoped_states(blocks, evm_states(pass_name, blocks))
